# Linux Shell Project

### Description of Project

This is a simple shell implementation in C, which allows users to execute commands, redirect input/output, and use pipes to connect multiple commands. The shell also keeps a history of previously entered commands and allows users to exit the shell by typing "exit".

### Instructions

To compile the shell, use the following command:
```
gcc -o myshell shell.c
```
To run the shell, use the following command:
```
./myshell
```
The shell will prompt the user to enter commands. To exit the shell, type "exit" and press Enter.
